    "body": "Based on:\n- #36716\n\nIf `errorSet` is reported for a socket we did not request to read from, disconnect directly instead. This just adds clarity: previously it would attempt a send that would then fail. The only side-effect is a changed log message. Since #36716, `select()` no longer reports errors for established connections, so this only applies to `poll()`.\n\nThe last commit does the same for HTTP, where on error it also no longer attempts a final read from a client whose reads are paused.\n\nAs a followup to #36716, `p2p_socket_errors.py` adds coverage for existing behavior:\n- the node ignores a single urgent byte: the connection stays open, ordinary data is still processed and the urgent byte is not counted as received.\n- a peer reset while the node is sending (the change above only changes the log message)\n\nSimilarly `interface_http.py` checks that:\n- a single urgent byte does not disturb an ordinary request.\n- a client reset while the server has unsent responses (the HTTP change only changes the log message)",
