      "message": "net: only use the select error set while connecting\n\nWindows uses the select() error set to report a failed non-blocking\nconnect(). Add ConnErrorEventFlag, which ConnectToSocket() passes to\nSock::Wait() to opt in to the error set while connecting. This is safe\non all platforms, as any error condition is worth waking for there.\n\nAll other uses of select() now leave the error set empty. With\nselect(), sockets waited on without the flag no longer wake up for or\nreport exceptional conditions, such as TCP urgent data on an\nestablished connection. No behavior change with poll().\n\nAdd a unit test: with an urgent byte pending, waiting for RecvEvent\nmust time out.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cory Fields <cory-nospam-@coryfields.com>",
